Lakṣmaṇa enters dreadful Kiṣkindhā cave at Rāma command --- Gate monkeys stand folded fearing breathing prince and bar not --- He beholds jewelled flowering cave with markets wish-trees perfumed wines --- He sees Mēru-Vindhya many-storied palaces rivers and chief houses on royal road --- He sees white women-jewelled houses and Mahēndra-like Sugrīva palace with guards --- He enters unopposed like sun into cloud passing seven courts to guarded harem --- He hears string song amid gold-silver couches beholding proud women and measured attendants --- He finds gold-hued Sugrīva on golden couch clasping Rumā and beholding him
